[ceiling] The lead-groove floor bridges the open channel when the convex +X face is on the bed. The groove is 5.6 mm wide, with a 6.8 mm maximum span at the cross-notches; its nominal 2.30 mm depth includes 0.25 mm for retained bridge strands. The 3.25 mm outer plateau supplies that allowance while preserving the floor at X=64.450, at least 0.8 mm of backing, and the glass bearing and tube seat. Supports are accessible through the outward-open groove.
